.Dd July 11, 2026
.Dt MESHD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm meshd
.Nd Bluetooth Mesh node daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl f Ar config
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
daemon is a Bluetooth Mesh node.
It holds the node's security material
.Pq NetKey, AppKey, IV Index, sequence number and Replay Protection List ,
registers the Generic OnOff and Generic Level application models and the
Configuration and Health foundation models, and processes access-layer
messages.
It is built on
.Xr libblemesh 3
and uses that library's
.Vt mesh_sim
network engine, driven as a single-node network, for the
receive, relay, reassembly and access-dispatch pipeline.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl d
Do not detach from the controlling terminal; run in the foreground.
.It Fl f Ar config
Read configuration from
.Ar config
instead of the default
.Pa /etc/bluetooth/meshd.conf .
.It Fl s Ar socket
Listen for control connections on
.Ar socket
instead of the default
.Pa /var/run/meshd.sock .
.El
.Sh CONTROL PROTOCOL
.Nm
serves a line-oriented control protocol on a
.Ux Ns -domain
stream socket.
The socket is created mode 0600, independent of the process umask.
On each accepted connection the daemon also verifies the peer credentials and
permits only root or a process running as the daemon's effective user.
Each request is one whitespace-separated command line; the reply is a single
line beginning with
.Ql OK
or
.Ql ERR .
The daemon services the listening socket, connected application sockets and
the blued bearer fd from one
.Xr kqueue 2
loop, so a long-lived application connection does not block other control
clients or inbound bearer traffic.
.Pp
Application model registrations made on a connected socket are scoped to that
connection.
When an inbound Access message matches a model registered by a
connection,
.Nm
queues the event on that connection and also writes an asynchronous
.Ql EVENT
line to the same socket.
The
.Cm app-events
command remains available for clients that prefer explicit queue draining.
The commands are:
.Bl -tag -width ".Cm provision-local Ar addr Ar iv"
.It Cm status
Report the node address, provisioning state, sequence number, IV Index,
current OnOff and Level state, default TTL and the receive/transmit counters.
.It Cm models
Report the local model inventory from the same Configuration Database used by
the Configuration Server.  Each entry lists the SIG model identifier, AppKey
binding count, subscription count and whether publication is configured.
Keys and publication labels are never included in this diagnostic view.
.It Cm app-register Ar element Ar model Op Ar vendor
Register an application-owned model on the specified local element.
The registration extends the local Configuration Database when necessary so
the model can receive AppKey bindings, subscriptions and publication state.
Registrations are per connected client; another application must register its
own models on its own socket.
.It Cm app-register-opcode Ar element Ar model Ar opcode Op Ar vendor
Register an opcode implemented by an application-owned model.
Unlike a model-only registration, this installs an explicit runtime dispatch
claim, allowing custom model messages to reach the owning client without
also delivering unrelated opcodes accepted by other models on the element.
.It Cm app-unregister Ar element Ar model Op Ar vendor
Remove a previously registered application-owned model.
.It Cm app-events Op Ar max
Drain queued inbound Access messages for registered application models.
Each event includes source, destination, opcode and parameter bytes.
Live application sockets also receive matching events as asynchronous
.Ql EVENT
lines.
.It Cm features
Report local node properties: Relay, Proxy, Friend and Low Power feature state, Secure
Network Beacon state, IV Index, local element addresses and sequence number.
.It Cm send Ar dst Ar appidx Ar access-hex
Originate a raw Access PDU to
.Ar dst
using the configured AppKey index.
The
.Ar access-hex
argument is the complete Access payload, including opcode and parameters.
.It Cm devkey-send Ar dst Ar remote Ns | Ns Ar local Ar netidx Ar access-hex
Originate a raw DevKey Access PDU to
.Ar dst .
Use
.Ar remote
to encrypt with the roster node's Device Key, or
.Ar local
to encrypt with this node's Device Key.
.It Cm publish Ar element Ar model Op Ar vendor Ar access-hex
Originate a raw Access PDU through the publication state configured for the
SIG model
.Ar model ,
or the vendor model identified by
.Ar vendor
and
.Ar model .
The source address is the specified local
.Ar element .
.It Cm onoff Ar dst Ar 0 Ns | Ns Ar 1
Originate an acknowledged Generic OnOff Set to
.Ar dst .
.It Cm level Ar dst Ar n
Originate an acknowledged Generic Level Set of
.Ar n
to
.Ar dst .
.It Cm power-onoff Ar dst Ar 0 Ns | Ns Ar 1 Ns | Ns Ar 2
Set the Generic OnPowerUp behavior of
.Ar dst
to Off, Default, or Restore.
.It Cm transition Ar dst Ar encoded-time
Set the Generic Default Transition Time.  The encoded octet uses the standard
two-bit resolution and six-bit step count; a step count of 63 is prohibited.
.It Cm power-level Ar dst Ar power
Set the Generic Power Actual state.
.It Cm power-default Ar dst Ar power
Set the Generic Power Default state.
.It Cm power-range Ar dst Ar min Ar max
Set the nonzero inclusive Generic Power Range.
.It Cm battery-state Ar level Ar discharge Ar charge Ar flags
Update the local Generic Battery state.  Times are 24-bit minute counts;
unknown values use the Mesh-defined all-ones encodings.
.It Cm location-global Ar latitude Ar longitude Ar altitude
Update the local Generic Location Global state using its signed wire units.
.It Cm location-local Ar north Ar east Ar altitude Ar floor Ar uncertainty
Update the local Generic Location Local state.
.It Cm sensor-set Ar property rawhex Op Ar pos neg sampling period interval
Register or update a Sensor property, descriptor, and current raw value.
.It Cm sensor-cadence Ar property divisor trigger down up min low high
Configure cadence; each raw threshold must match the registered value width.
.It Cm sensor-setting Ar property setting 1|3 rawhex
Register a read-only or read/write Sensor setting.
.It Cm sensor-column Ar property keyhex rawhex
Register a bounded Sensor Series column.
.It Cm time-set Ar tai subsecond uncertainty authority delta zone
Set the local Mesh Time state using the standard 40-bit TAI Seconds and
15-bit encoded TAI-UTC Delta fields.
.It Cm time-role Ar 0..3
Set the local Time Role.
.It Cm time-zone Ar offset change-tai
Schedule the new Time Zone Offset at the specified TAI instant.
.It Cm time-delta Ar delta change-tai
Schedule the new encoded TAI-UTC Delta at the specified TAI instant.
.It Cm scene-store Ar scene-number
Store the bound Generic OnOff, Generic Level, and Generic Power Actual states
as a local Scene.
.It Cm scene-recall Ar scene-number
Recall a stored local Scene.
.It Cm scene-delete Ar scene-number
Delete a local Scene; deleting a non-existent scene succeeds as specified.
.It Cm scheduler-set Ar index year months day hour minute second dow action transition scene
Set a local Scheduler register entry using the Mesh field encodings.  Action
15 clears the entry.
.It Cm lightness-state Ar actual
Set the local Light Lightness Actual state and its required Generic OnOff and
Generic Level bindings.
.It Cm lightness-default Ar value
Set the local Light Lightness Default state.
.It Cm lightness-range Ar min max
Set the nonzero inclusive local Light Lightness Range.
.It Cm ctl-state Ar lightness temperature delta-uv
Set the local Light CTL state, including its Light Lightness binding.
.It Cm ctl-range Ar min-temperature max-temperature
Set the local Light CTL Temperature Range; values must be within 800 to 20000 K.
.It Cm hsl-state Ar lightness hue saturation
Set the local Light HSL state and its Light Lightness binding.
.It Cm hsl-range Ar hue-min hue-max sat-min sat-max
Set the inclusive Hue and Saturation ranges for the local HSL server.
.It Cm xyl-state Ar lightness x y
Set the local Light xyL state and its Light Lightness binding.
.It Cm xyl-range Ar x-min x-max y-min y-max
Set the inclusive x and y ranges for the local xyL server.
.It Cm lc-mode Ar 0|1
Set the local Light LC Mode state.
.It Cm lc-om Ar 0|1
Set the local Light LC Occupancy Mode state.
.It Cm lc-light-onoff Ar 0|1
Set the local Light LC Light OnOff state and apply the bound Light Lightness
state when LC Mode is enabled.
.It Cm lc-property Ar property rawhex
Set a local Light LC property value.
.It Cm ttl Ar n
Set the default Time To Live
.Pq 0..127, not 1 .
.It Cm attention Ar secs
Set the Health server attention timer.
.It Cm provision-local Ar addr Ar iv
Self-provision the node at unicast address
.Ar addr
with IV Index
.Ar iv ,
using the configured NetKey.
.It Cm create-network
Mint a new mesh network, making this node the Provisioner and Configuration
Client.
.It Cm list-nodes
List the provisioned-node roster managed by the local Provisioner.
.It Cm import-remote-node Ar primary Ar count Ar devkey-hex32
Import a remote node that was provisioned outside
.Nm
into the local Provisioner roster.
.Ar primary
is the node's primary unicast address,
.Ar count
is the number of elements, and
.Ar devkey-hex32
is the 16-octet Device Key.
.It Cm delete-remote-node Ar primary Ar count
Delete a remote node record from the local Provisioner roster.
.It Cm provision-scan Oo Cm on | Cm off | Cm list Oc
Control unprovisioned-device discovery.
With
.Cm on
(the default when no argument is given) discovery is enabled and the result
cache is cleared; Unprovisioned Device Beacons received on the bearer are then
parsed and their device UUIDs recorded.
.Cm list
reports the currently discovered UUIDs without disturbing the scan, and
.Cm off
disables discovery.
The reply lists the active flag, the device count and each discovered UUID; feed
a UUID to
.Cm provision .
.It Cm provision-oob Oo Ar hex | Cm output | Cm input | Cm both | Cm none Oc
Configure the out-of-band authentication of the next provisioning
.Pq Mesh Protocol 1.1.1 Section 5.4.1.3, Table 5.31 .
.Pp
.Ar hex
installs the Static OOB authentication value
.Pq Authentication Method 0x01
of the device that is about to be provisioned: the out-of-band octet array
supplied by the device manufacturer - printed on the label, packed in the
carton or read from an NFC tag - as 2 to 64 hexadecimal digits.
.Pp
.Cm output ,
.Cm input
and
.Cm both
opt in to the two operator-driven methods, Output OOB
.Pq 0x02
and Input OOB
.Pq 0x03 .
They are off by default because each stalls the exchange on a human:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
With Output OOB the Provisionee generates a value and outputs it - blinking,
beeping, vibrating or displaying it - and the operator hands it back with
.Cm provision-oob-input
.Pq Section 5.4.2.4.3 .
.It
With Input OOB
.Nm
generates the value, reports it as a display prompt, and the operator enters it
on the device; the device answers with a Provisioning Input Complete PDU
.Pq Section 5.4.2.4.4 .
.El
.Pp
The pending prompt is reported by this verb with no argument and is pushed to
every connected control client as a
.Dq prov-oob-display
or
.Dq prov-oob-input
app event carrying the Authentication Action, the Authentication Size and, for
a display prompt, the value itself.
An unanswered prompt fails the provisioning after 60 seconds
.Pq Section 5.4.4 .
.Pp
All settings apply to every subsequent
.Cm provision
and
.Cm provision-gatt
until they are cleared with
.Cm none ,
so a batch of identical devices is provisioned with one setting.
With no argument the current setting and any pending prompt are reported.
.Pp
The strongest method the peer's Provisioning Capabilities and the local
settings both permit is selected: Static OOB first, then Output OOB, then Input
OOB.
An authenticated method is never silently downgraded to an unauthenticated one:
a peer that advertises
.Dq only OOB authenticated provisioning supported
and for which no method can be selected is refused, and a Provisioning Start
that selects an Action or a Size this node did not advertise is refused as
well.
Without any OOB method the exchange is unauthenticated
.Pq Authentication Method 0x00
and a man in the middle within radio range can learn the NetKey and the Device
Key.
.It Cm provision-oob-input Ar value
Answer a pending Output OOB prompt with the value the peer displayed
.Pq Mesh Protocol 1.1.1 Section 5.4.2.4.3 ,
resuming the stalled provisioning: the Provisioning Confirmation computed from
the resulting AuthValue is sent immediately.
A numeric
.Ar value
may be typed without its leading zeros; an alphanumeric one is exactly the
announced number of characters from the set 0-9 and A-Z.
A value that does not match the negotiated Authentication Action and
Authentication Size is rejected without disturbing the session, so the operator
can retype it.
.It Cm provision Ar uuid-hex32 Op Ar elements
Provision an unprovisioned peer over PB-ADV.
.It Cm provision-status
Poll and commit an in-flight PB-ADV or PB-GATT provisioning session.
.It Cm provision-gatt Ar addr Oo Cm public | Cm random Oc Op Cm adapter= Ns Ar index
.Ar uuid-hex32 Op Ar elements
Provision a connected peer over PB-GATT.
The peer must expose the Mesh
Provisioning Service (0x1827); characteristic discovery, Data Out subscription,
Data In writes and Proxy-PDU segmentation are handled through
.Xr blued 8 .
The address type defaults to
.Cm public
when omitted.
When the same peer identity is connected through more than one controller,
.Cm adapter= Ns Ar index
selects the controller explicitly; otherwise the sole matching connection is
selected automatically.
.It Cm proxy-gatt Ar addr Oo Cm public | Cm random Oc Op Cm adapter= Ns Ar index
Open a Mesh Proxy GATT connection.
.It Cm proxy-gatt-close Ar addr Oo Cm public | Cm random Oc Op Cm adapter= Ns Ar index
Close the selected Mesh Proxy GATT connection.
.It Cm proxy-filter-set Ar addr Oo Cm public | Cm random Oc
.Op Cm adapter= Ns Ar index
.Ar net-idx Cm accept | Cm reject
Set the Proxy filter type.
.It Cm proxy-filter-add Ar addr Oo Cm public | Cm random Oc
.Op Cm adapter= Ns Ar index
.Ar net-idx Ar mesh-addr ...
Add addresses to the Proxy filter.
.It Cm proxy-filter-remove Ar addr Oo Cm public | Cm random Oc
.Op Cm adapter= Ns Ar index
.Ar net-idx Ar mesh-addr ...
Remove addresses from the Proxy filter.
.Pp
The optional adapter selector has the same meaning as for
.Cm provision-gatt .
.It Cm reset
Return the node to the unprovisioned state.
.It Cm key-refresh Cm begin | advance | finish | status | network | network-status
Drive Key Refresh on the primary subnet.
.Cm begin
starts a refresh (distributing a new NetKey),
.Cm advance
moves to the next phase,
.Cm finish
completes it, and
.Cm status
reports the current phase.
.Cm network
and
.Cm network-status
operate the network-wide refresh the local Provisioner coordinates across the
roster.
.It Cm friend Oo Cm on | off | status Oc
Toggle the Friend role.
When enabled, the node accepts a Friend Request from a neighbouring Low Power
node, answers it with a Friend Offer, maintains a Friend Queue of messages
destined for that node, and delivers the queued messages (and Friend Updates)
in response to each Friend Poll, all over the advertising bearer
.Pq Xr MshPRT 1.1 Sx 3.6.6 .
With no argument (or
.Cm status )
the current role state is reported.
.It Cm low-power Oo Cm on | off | status Oc
Toggle the Low Power node role.
When enabled, the node originates a Friend Request on its next tick, selects a
Friend from the returned Offers, establishes the friendship, and thereafter
polls the Friend on a fixed cadence to retrieve queued messages, re-establishing
if the PollTimeout lapses
.Pq Xr MshPRT 1.1 Sx 3.6.5 .
.El
.Ss Config Client
The
.Cm cfg
family drives a provisioned roster node's Configuration Server by sending
acknowledged Configuration messages sealed under that node's Device Key and
surfacing the returned Config Status.
Every sub-verb takes the destination node's primary unicast address as its first
argument.
A network must exist
.Pq Cm create-network
first.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm cfg comp-get Ar dst Op Ar page
Composition Data Get.
.It Cm cfg appkey-add | appkey-update | appkey-delete Ar dst
AppKey Add, Update or Delete (primary AppKey).
.It Cm cfg appkey-get Ar dst Ar netidx
AppKey Get.
.It Cm cfg model-bind | model-unbind | model-app-get Ar dst Ar elem Ar model Op Ar company
Model AppKey Bind, Unbind or Get.
.It Cm cfg sub-add | sub-delete | sub-overwrite Ar dst Ar elem Ar group Ar model Op Ar company
Model Subscription Add, Delete or Overwrite.
.It Cm cfg sub-delete-all Ar dst Ar elem Ar model Op Ar company
Model Subscription Delete All.
.It Cm cfg sub-va-add | sub-va-delete | sub-va-overwrite Ar dst Ar elem Ar label-hex32 Ar model Op Ar company
Model Subscription Virtual Address Add, Delete or Overwrite.
.It Cm cfg sub-get Ar dst Ar elem Ar model Op Ar company
Model Subscription Get.
.It Cm cfg pub-set Ar dst Ar elem Ar pubaddr Ar ttl Ar period Ar rtx Ar model Op Ar company
Model Publication Set.
.It Cm cfg pub-va-set Ar dst Ar elem Ar label-hex32 Ar ttl Ar period Ar rtx Ar model Op Ar company
Model Publication Virtual Address Set.
.It Cm cfg pub-get Ar dst Ar elem Ar model Op Ar company
Model Publication Get.
.It Cm cfg netkey-add | netkey-update Ar dst Ar netidx Ar key-hex32
NetKey Add or Update.
.It Cm cfg netkey-delete Ar dst Ar netidx
NetKey Delete.
.It Cm cfg kr-phase-get Ar dst Ar netidx
Key Refresh Phase Get.
.It Cm cfg kr-phase-set Ar dst Ar netidx Ar transition
Key Refresh Phase Set.
.It Cm cfg beacon | gatt-proxy | friend | ttl | relay | nettransmit Ar dst Op Ar value ...
Get or Set the named node-wide state (omit the value to Get).
.It Cm cfg node-identity-get Ar dst Ar netidx
Node Identity Get.
.It Cm cfg node-identity-set Ar dst Ar netidx Ar identity
Node Identity Set.
.It Cm cfg lpn-polltimeout-get Ar dst Ar lpn-addr
Low Power Node PollTimeout Get.
.It Cm cfg hb-pub-get Ar dst
Heartbeat Publication Get.
.It Cm cfg hb-pub-set Ar dst Ar hbdst Ar countlog Ar periodlog Ar ttl Ar netidx
Heartbeat Publication Set.
.It Cm cfg hb-sub-get Ar dst
Heartbeat Subscription Get.
.It Cm cfg hb-sub-set Ar dst Ar src Ar hbdst Ar periodlog
Heartbeat Subscription Set.
.It Cm cfg sar-tx-get | sar-rx-get Ar dst
SAR Transmitter or Receiver Get.
.It Cm cfg sar-tx-set Ar dst Ar segint Ar ucount Ar unoprog Ar uintstep Ar uintinc Ar mcount Ar mintstep
SAR Transmitter Set (seven 4-bit fields).
.It Cm cfg sar-rx-set Ar dst Ar segthresh Ar ackdelayinc Ar discard Ar rxintstep Ar ackretrans
SAR Receiver Set.
.It Cm cfg priv-beacon-get Ar dst
Private Beacon Get.
.It Cm cfg priv-beacon-set Ar dst Ar 0 Ns | Ns Ar 1 Op Ar random-update-steps
Private Beacon Set.
.It Cm cfg priv-gatt-proxy Ar dst Op Ar value
Private GATT Proxy Get or Set.
.It Cm cfg od-priv-proxy Ar dst Op Ar value
On-Demand Private Proxy Get or Set.
.It Cm cfg priv-node-identity-get Ar dst Ar netidx
Private Node Identity Get.
.It Cm cfg priv-node-identity-set Ar dst Ar netidx Ar identity
Private Node Identity Set.
.It Cm cfg lcd-get Ar dst Ar page Ar offset
Large Composition Data Get.
.It Cm cfg node-reset Ar dst
Node Reset: remove the node from the network and clear its provisioning.
.El
.Ss Directed Forwarding
.Nm
registers a Directed Forwarding Configuration Server (answering the
Directed Control, Path Metric, Directed Wanted Lanes, Two Way Path,
Path Echo Interval and Directed Network Transmit / Relay Retransmit states)
and drives a Path Origin path-discovery FSM.
The
.Cm df
verbs operate a remote node's DF Configuration Server over its DevKey and drive
the local discovery FSM
.Pq MshMDL_v1.1 Section 4.4.3 :
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It Cm df get Ar dst Op Ar netidx
Directed Control Get.
.It Cm df set Ar dst Cm on Ns | Ns Cm off Op Ar netidx
Directed Control Set (directed forwarding + directed relay).
.It Cm df control-set Ar dst Ar netidx Ar fwd Ar relay Ar proxy Ar proxydef Ar friend
Directed Control Set with all five flags.
Each flag is
.Cm 0
(Disable),
.Cm 1
(Enable) or
.Cm 0xff
(Do Not Process).
.Ar proxydef
must be
.Cm 0xff
whenever
.Ar proxy
is
.Cm 0xff :
a value depending on a state the Set is not processing is Prohibited
(MshMDL Table 4.199) and the Configuration Server drops such a message
without answering.
.It Cm df metric-get | metric-set Ar dst Ar ...
Path Metric Get/Set.
.It Cm df lanes-get | lanes-set Ar dst Ar ...
Directed Wanted Lanes Get/Set.
.It Cm df two-way-get | two-way-set Ar dst Ar ...
Two Way Path Get/Set.
.It Cm df echo-get | echo-set Ar dst Ar ...
Path Echo Interval Get/Set.
.It Cm df net-transmit-get | net-transmit-set Ar dst Ar ...
Directed Network Transmit Get/Set.
.It Cm df relay-retransmit-get | relay-retransmit-set Ar dst Ar ...
Directed Relay Retransmit Get/Set.
.It Cm df discover Ar target
Start a local Path Origin path discovery toward
.Ar target ;
the reply/confirmation exchange advances the FSM to established and the node
tick ages the forwarding table and fails a timed-out discovery.
.It Cm df discover-status
Report the local path-discovery FSM state.
.El
.Ss Subnet Bridge
.Nm
can act as a Subnet Bridge: a node that retransmits a Network PDU received on
one subnet onto a different subnet, re-securing it with that subnet's network
credentials
.Pq MshPRT_v1.1.1 Section 3.4.6.3 .
It registers a Bridge Configuration Server
.Pq Section 4.4.9
on the primary element, which owns three states:
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It Subnet Bridge
.Pq Section 4.2.41
Disabled
.Pq Li 0x00 ,
the default, or enabled
.Pq Li 0x01 .
.It Bridging Table
.Pq Section 4.2.42
A list of entries, each pairing two NetKey Indexes with two addresses and the
directions in which traffic between them may cross.
Empty by default.
.It Bridging Table Size
.Pq Section 4.2.43
The maximum number of entries, 16 here
.Pq the specification requires at least 16 .
.El
.Pp
A Network PDU crosses when a Bridging Table entry names its source address as
Address1, its destination address as Address2 and the subnet that secured it as
NetKeyIndex1; it is then retransmitted under NetKeyIndex2.
The reverse crossing, from Address2 to Address1 under NetKeyIndex2 and out on
NetKeyIndex1, additionally requires the entry's Directions value to be
.Li 0x02 .
The retransmitted PDU keeps the original source address, sequence number and IV
Index and carries a TTL one less than the received PDU: a bridge re-secures a
message, it does not originate one, so its own sequence number is not consumed
and the far end still authenticates against the originator's SeqAuth.
.Pp
Bridged traffic is replay-protected by a list separate from the node's own
replay protection list, keyed by source address across both subnets
.Pq Section 3.9.8 .
A message whose IVISeq is not strictly newer than the stored value for its
source is discarded on reception and is not bridged; the stored value advances
only when the message is actually retransmitted onto the bridged subnet.
.Pp
Deleting a NetKey removes every Bridging Table entry naming its NetKey Index in
either position
.Pq Section 4.2.42.1 .
Both the Subnet Bridge state and the Bridging Table state are persisted.
.Pp
Bridge messages
.Pq Section 4.3.11
are secured with the node's DevKey, and the access-layer security on the Bridge
Configuration Server model is the device key
.Pq Section 4.4.9.1 .
A Bridge message that arrives secured with a bound AppKey is refused and
counted; see
.Cm bridge stats .
The
.Cm bridge
verbs configure this node's own Bridge Configuration Server by submitting the
corresponding Section 4.3.11 message to it, so the operator path and the
over-the-air path run the same server code:
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It Cm bridge Op Cm status
Report the Subnet Bridge state, the number of Bridging Table entries and the
Bridging Table Size state
.Pq SUBNET_BRIDGE_GET .
.It Cm bridge on | off
Enable or disable subnet bridge functionality
.Pq SUBNET_BRIDGE_SET .
.It Cm bridge add Ar netidx1 Ar netidx2 Ar addr1 Ar addr2 Ar directions
Add or update a Bridging Table entry
.Pq BRIDGING_TABLE_ADD .
.Ar directions
is
.Cm 1
(only
.Ar addr1
to
.Ar addr2 )
or
.Cm 2
(both ways).
.Ar addr1
must be a unicast address, the two NetKey Indexes must differ, and the two
addresses must differ;
.Ar addr2
must be a unicast address when
.Ar directions
is
.Cm 2 .
.It Cm bridge remove Ar netidx1 Ar netidx2 Ar addr1 Ar addr2
Remove Bridging Table entries
.Pq BRIDGING_TABLE_REMOVE .
Either address may be
.Cm 0
(the unassigned address), which matches any address in that position.
.It Cm bridge list Ar netidx1 Ar netidx2 Op Ar start
List the bridged addresses and directions of one pair of subnets
.Pq BRIDGING_TABLE_GET .
.It Cm bridge subnets Op Ar filter Op Ar netidx Op Ar start
List the bridged pairs of NetKey Indexes
.Pq BRIDGED_SUBNETS_GET .
.Ar filter
is
.Cm 0
(all pairs),
.Cm 1
.Pq Ar netidx No matches NetKeyIndex1 ,
.Cm 2
.Pq Ar netidx No matches NetKeyIndex2
or
.Cm 3
.Pq either .
.It Cm bridge size
Report the Bridging Table Size state
.Pq BRIDGING_TABLE_SIZE_GET .
.It Cm bridge stats
Report the number of PDUs bridged, the number dropped by the bridge replay
list, and the number of AppKey-secured Bridge messages refused.
.El
.Pp
Only the flooding outbound path of MshPRT_v1.1.1 Table 3.14 is implemented.
Every "Traffic is to be bridged" row of that table is written conjoined with
"Directed forwarding is enabled", but Section 3.4.6.3's own prose imposes no
such condition and the Bridge Configuration Server has no dependency on the
Directed Forwarding feature, so bridging here works in a flooding-only network.
The directed outbound rows, which retransmit on path bearers with directed
security credentials, are not implemented, and neither is the Section 3.6.8.1.11
treatment of bridged addresses as dependent nodes of the Subnet Bridge.
.Ss Remote Provisioning
.Nm
registers a Remote Provisioning Server (the Scan and Link control of the
Remote Provisioning Server model) and drives a Remote Provisioning Client.
The
.Cm remote-prov
verbs operate a remote Remote Provisioning Server over its DevKey
.Pq MshPRT_v1.1 Section 5.4.4 :
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It Cm remote-prov caps Ar dst
Scan Capabilities Get.
.It Cm remote-prov scan Ar dst Op Ar uuid-hex32 Op Ar limit Ar timeout
Scan Start (a device UUID targets a single device).
.It Cm remote-prov scan-get | scan-stop Ar dst
Scan Get / Scan Stop.
.It Cm remote-prov link-get Ar dst
Link Get.
.It Cm remote-prov link-open Ar dst Ar uuid-hex32 Op Ar timeout
Open a PB-Remote provisioning link toward a device through the server.
.It Cm remote-prov provision Ar dst Ar uuid-hex32 Op Ar timeout
Alias for
.Cm link-open .
.It Cm remote-prov link-close Ar dst Op Ar reason
Link Close.
.It Cm remote-prov status
Report the Remote Provisioning client scan/link FSM state.
.It Cm remote-prov reports
List the unsolicited Reports (Scan Report, Link Report, PDU Report) the Client
has received from a Server.
.El
.Pp
When
.Nm
acts as a Remote Provisioning Server it emits unsolicited Scan/Link/PDU Reports
to the Client that addressed it; as a Client it decodes those Reports, drives its
scan/link FSMs and the inbound PDU tunnel, and buffers them for
.Cm remote-prov reports .
.Sh BEARER INTEGRATION
.Nm
uses
.Xr blued 8
as its privileged radio broker.
The bearer remains an explicit integration seam
.Pq Vt struct meshd_bearer :
outbound secured Network PDUs are handed to a transmit callback and inbound
frames are delivered with
.Fn meshd_bearer_rx .
The current brokered bearer carries:
.Bl -bullet
.It
The
.Em advertising bearer :
LE non-connectable advertising and passive scanning for the Mesh Message
.Pq AD type 0x2A ,
Mesh Beacon
.Pq 0x2B
and PB-ADV
.Pq 0x29
AD structures, via the HCI socket already used by
.Xr blued 8 .
.It
PB-GATT provisioning through the Mesh Provisioning Service
.Pq 0x1827 ,
using Data In UUID 0x2ADB and Data Out UUID 0x2ADC over
.Xr blued 8
ATT operations.
.El
.Pp
One bearer remains future work:
.Bl -bullet
.It
The
.Em GATT Proxy bearer :
the Mesh Proxy Service
.Pq 0x1828
with its Data In / Data Out characteristics, exposed through the
.Xr blued 8
ATT server, with proxy-PDU SAR handled by the
.Vt mesh_proxy
module of
.Xr libblemesh 3 .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ".Pa /usr/share/examples/meshd/meshd.conf.sample" -compact
.It Pa /etc/bluetooth/meshd.conf
Default configuration file.
When it contains a
.Cm netkey
or
.Cm appkey
directive, the file must be owned by the daemon's effective user and must not
grant any group or other permissions (normally mode 0600).
.It Pa /var/run/meshd.sock
Default control socket.
.It Pa /usr/share/examples/meshd/meshd.conf.sample
Annotated sample configuration.
.El
.Sh DTRACE
When built with
.Va MESHD_DTRACE_PROBES
and DTrace enabled,
.Nm
exposes the
.Ql meshd
USDT provider with probes for application socket connect, disconnect,
registration, event queue, event drop and event send paths.
The probes carry file descriptors, model identifiers, opcodes and queue
counters only; key material and Access payload bytes are not traced.
